{"name":"Whole Grain","hex":"#d4ae7e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"whole grain","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of wholegrain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whole_grain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whole grain","blocks":[{"text":"A whole grain is a grain of any cereal or pseudocereal that contains the endosperm, germ, and bran, in contrast to refined grains, which retain only the endosperm."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Wheat-kernel_nutrition.svg/330px-Wheat-kernel_nutrition.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whole_grain","wikidata":"Q1938952"},{"title":"Grain","blocks":[{"text":"A grain is a small, hard, dry fruit (caryopsis)–with or without an attached hull layer–harvested for human or animal consumption. A grain crop is a grain-producing plant. The two main types of commercial grain crops are cereals and legumes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Dhaniyangal.jpg/330px-Dhaniyangal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grain","wikidata":"Q2995529"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Reis_-_Sorte_C_roh.jpg/250px-Reis_-_Sorte_C_roh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Reis_-_Sorte_C_roh.jpg/500px-Reis_-_Sorte_C_roh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Reis_-_Sorte_C_roh.jpg/250px-Reis_-_Sorte_C_roh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AReis_-_Sorte_C_roh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Reis_-